  '["Because the concentration of dissolved oxygen in water is very low compared to oxygen in air, aquatic animals must breathe much faster to take in sufficient oxygen.","The amount of dissolved oxygen in water is fairly small compared to air, so aquatic organisms breathe rapidly to extract enough oxygen."]'::jsonb,
