  '["Volatile chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) are released from refrigeration equipment into the troposphere.","Unreactive CFC molecules gradually diffuse upward across the tropopause into the stratosphere.","High-energy solar ultraviolet (UV) radiation breaks carbon-chlorine bonds, releasing free chlorine radicals (Cl·).","Chlorine radicals react with ozone (O3), breaking it into chlorine monoxide and diatomic oxygen (O2).","Continuous catalytic ozone destruction creates a thinned ozone hole, allowing harmful UVB radiation to penetrate Earth''s surface."]'::jsonb,
  'Ozone destruction cycle: Release of CFCs -> Diffusion to stratosphere -> Photodissociation by UV -> Catalytic ozone breakdown -> Increased surface UVB penetration.'
) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET
