  NULL,
  0.2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'Molar mass of Fe₂O₃ = 2(56) + 3(16) = 160 g/mol. Moles of Fe₂O₃ = 80.0 / 160 = 0.50 mol. Stoichiometric ratio: 1 mol Fe₂O₃ requires 2 mol Al. Therefore, 0.50 mol Fe₂O₃ requires 1.0 mol Al. Molar mass of Al = 27 g/mol. Mass of Al = 1.0 mol × 27 g/mol = 27.0 g.'
