  'c10-chemistry-074',
  '"ordered"'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  '["Methane [CH₄, boiling point -161 °C]","Ethane [C₂H₆, boiling point -89 °C]","Propane [C₃H₈, boiling point -42 °C]","Butane [C₄H₁₀, boiling point -0.5 °C]","Pentane [C₅H₁₂, boiling point 36 °C]"]'::jsonb,
  'As carbon chain length and molecular mass increase, molecular surface area expands, leading to stronger intermolecular London dispersion forces and higher boiling points: CH₄ < C₂H₆ < C₃H₈ < C₄H₁₀ < C₅H₁₂.'
