  'c10-physics-044',
  '0'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'Filament lamps operate by emitting thermal radiation when heated to incandescent temperatures (>2500 °C). Tungsten''s ultra-high melting point (3380 °C) and high resistance allow it to retain Joule heat without melting or disintegrating.'
