  'Object distance u = -20 cm, focal length f = -15 cm. Mirror formula: 1/v = 1/f - 1/u = -1/15 - (-1/20) = -1/15 + 1/20 = (-4 + 3)/60 = -1/60 => v = -60 cm. Magnification m = -v / u = -(-60) / (-20) = -3. Image height h'' = m × h = -3 × 5 cm = -15 cm.'
