  '0'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'In bryophytes (mosses and liverworts), the dominant photosynthetic, independent plant body is the haploid gametophyte; the diploid sporophyte is parasitic or partially dependent on it. In pteridophytes (ferns), the dominant independent plant body is the vascular diploid sporophyte, while the gametophyte (prothallus) is small and short-lived.'
