  'c11-biology-018',
  NULL,
  '["they completely lack a cell wall, whereas penicillin acts by inhibiting bacterial cell wall synthesis","penicillin targets peptidoglycan cell wall synthesis which Mycoplasma lacks","they have no cell wall for penicillin to target"]'::jsonb,
  '["lack","cell wall","penicillin","peptidoglycan","synthesis"]'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'Mycoplasma (PPLO) are the smallest known living cells and completely lack a cell wall. Because beta-lactam antibiotics like penicillin inhibit bacterial cell wall cross-linking, they have no target in Mycoplasma and are ineffective.'
