) VALUES (
  'c11-biology-095',
  NULL,
  '["steroid hormones cross the cell membrane and bind intracellular receptors to alter gene expression; peptide hormones bind surface receptors and generate second messengers","steroid hormones act via intracellular receptors and regulate transcription; peptide hormones act via membrane receptors and second messengers like cAMP"]'::jsonb,
  '["steroid","intracellular receptors","gene expression","peptide","membrane receptors","second messengers"]'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'Steroid hormones (estrogen, cortisol) are lipophilic and cross membranes to bind nuclear receptor proteins that interact with hormone response elements on DNA. Peptide hormones are hydrophilic and rely on membrane receptor activation coupled to second messenger cascades.'
