  'c11-chemistry-080',
  '0'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'Geometrical isomerism requires restricted rotation about the C=C bond and each doubly bonded carbon atom must be attached to two different groups. In but-2-ene (CH₃-CH=CH-CH₃), each C has an -H and a -CH₃ group, allowing cis and trans isomers. In but-1-ene, propene, and 2-methylpropene, one of the alkene carbons has two identical groups.'
