  0.1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  '22400 mL of N₂ at STP has a mass of 28 g. Therefore, 22.4 mL of N₂ at STP has mass = (28 / 22400) × 22.4 = 0.028 g. Percentage of nitrogen = (mass of N₂ / mass of compound) × 100 = (0.028 / 0.28) × 100 = 10%.'
