  'c11-chemistry-094',
  NULL,
  '["both propagation steps are exothermic only for HBr; for HCl H-Cl bond is too strong and for HI iodine radicals dimerize into I2","H-Cl bond is too strong to break homolytically, while I-H bond breaking produces iodine radicals that dimerize to form I2","only for HBr are both propagation steps exothermic; endothermic for HCl and HI"]'::jsonb,
  '["propagation steps","exothermic","H-Cl","bond","dimerize","iodine"]'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'In the free radical mechanism of addition to alkenes, both propagation steps are exothermic only for HBr. For HCl, the H-Cl bond dissociation energy is very high (step 1 endothermic). For HI, iodine atoms preferentially combine to form I₂ rather than adding to the alkene double bond (step 2 endothermic).'
