  'c11-maths-007',
  11,
  'maths',
  'Sets',
  'truefalse',
  'easy',
  'According to De Morgan''s laws of set theory, the complement of the union of any two sets equals the intersection of their individual complements: (A ∪ B)'' = A'' ∩ B''.',
