  'logic',
  'hard',
  'Evaluate the Assertion (A) and Reason (R):
Assertion (A): For any two arbitrary events A and B in a sample space, P(A ∪ B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A ∩ B).
Reason (R): When summing P(A) and P(B), the probability of the simultaneous occurrence P(A ∩ B) is counted twice and must be subtracted once by the principle of inclusion-exclusion.',
  '["Both (A) and (R) are true, and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).","Both (A) and (R) are true, but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A).","(A) is true, but (R) is false.","(A) is false, but (R) is true."]'::jsonb,
