  'mcq',
  'hard',
  'A river 400 m wide flows east at 3 m/s. A swimmer who swims at 5 m/s in still water intends to cross directly along the shortest perpendicular path across the river bank. In which direction must the swimmer head, and how long does the crossing take?',
  '["At an angle of sin⁻¹(0.6) = 37° upstream from the perpendicular, taking 100 s","Perpendicular to the river current, taking 80 s","At 45° upstream, taking 120 s","At 60° upstream, taking 150 s"]'::jsonb,
