  'physics',
  'Mechanical Properties of Fluids',
  'mcq',
  'hard',
  'Water flows through a horizontal pipe of non-uniform cross-section. At section 1 of diameter d₁ = 4 cm, the flow speed is v₁ = 2 m/s. At section 2, the diameter narrows to d₂ = 2 cm. What is the flow speed v₂ and how does the static pressure P₂ compare to P₁?',
  '["v₂ = 8 m/s, static pressure decreases (P₂ < P₁)","v₂ = 4 m/s, static pressure increases (P₂ > P₁)","v₂ = 8 m/s, static pressure increases (P₂ > P₁)","v₂ = 1 m/s, static pressure decreases (P₂ < P₁)"]'::jsonb,
