  'mcq',
  'medium',
  'During microsporogenesis in an anther, the innermost wall layer that surrounds the sporogenous tissue is the tapetum. Which of the following is a primary physiological characteristic and function of tapetal cells?',
  '["They are multinucleate with dense cytoplasm, nourish developing microspores, and secrete sporopollenin precursors and pollen kitt","They are dry, fibrous, dead cells that assist in mechanical dehiscence of the anther","They undergo meiosis directly to produce microspore tetrads","They act as protective epidermal cells preventing pathogen entry"]'::jsonb,
