  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'The tapetum is the innermost nourishing anther wall layer. Its cells possess dense cytoplasm and often become multinucleate or polyploid due to endomitosis. Tapetum supplies nutrients to developing pollen grains and secretes enzymes, hormones, sporopollenin precursors, and sticky pollen kitt.'
