  'The Haworth structure shows a cyclic hemiacetal pyranose form of D-glucose. What is this specific anomer called, characterized by the hydroxyl group at C-1 (anomeric carbon) pointing downward (trans to -CH2OH at C-5)?',
  '["alpha-D-Glucopyranose","beta-D-Glucopyranose","alpha-D-Fructofuranose","beta-D-Galactopyranose"]'::jsonb,
  '{"kind":"svg","src":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 200\" width=\"100%\" height=\"160\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polygon points=\"160,50 230,80 230,140 160,170 90,140 90,80\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#0284c7\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#0284c7\">O</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"145\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#ef4444\">C1 — OH (down)</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#16a34a\">CH₂OH (up at C5)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1e293b\">D-Glucopyranose ring</text></svg>"}'::jsonb,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  1,
