  NULL,
  'In D-glucopyranose, the anomer with the C-1 hydroxyl group in the downward direction (trans to the -CH2OH group at C-5) is alpha-D-(+)-glucopyranose. When the -OH is upward (cis), it is beta-D-(+)-glucopyranose.'
