  'Because water is present in enormous excess, its concentration remains practically unchanged throughout the reaction ([H2O] approx constant). The rate law reduces to Rate = k''[H2O][ester] = k[ester], which is called a pseudo-first-order reaction.'
) ON CONFLICT (question_id) DO UPDATE SET
