  'chemistry',
  'The d- and f-Block Elements',
  'mcq',
  'hard',
  'In aqueous solution, the interconversion between yellow chromate ion (CrO4 2-) and orange dichromate ion (Cr2O7 2-) depends on pH according to: 2 CrO4 2- + 2 H+ <=> Cr2O7 2- + H2O. What happens to the oxidation state of chromium during this pH-dependent colour change?',
  '["It remains unchanged at +6 in both chromate and dichromate ions","It changes from +6 in chromate to +3 in dichromate","It changes from +3 in chromate to +6 in dichromate","It changes from +7 to +6"]'::jsonb,
