  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'Cyanide ion (:C≡N:⁻) is an ambident nucleophile. In ionic KCN, both C and N can attack, but C-attack is favoured because the C-C bond is much stronger than C-N. In covalent Ag-C≡N, the carbon is engaged in bonding with silver, so the nitrogen lone pair attacks to form alkyl isocyanide.'
