  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'In intrinsic semiconductors: as temperature increases, more covalent bonds break, generating more electron-hole pairs (n_i increases exponentially with T). Therefore, conductivity sigma increases and resistivity rho decreases, giving a negative temperature coefficient of resistance (alpha < 0). The Fermi level remains near the center of the band gap.'
