  'physics',
  'Nuclei',
  'mcq',
  'medium',
  'From the binding energy per nucleon (E_bn) versus mass number (A) curve, what can be deduced about nuclear stability?',
  '["E_bn is maximum around A = 56 (Iron) with a value of about 8.75 MeV/nucleon, making intermediate nuclei most stable","E_bn increases monotonically with mass number A, making super-heavy nuclei the most stable","Very light nuclei (A < 20) have higher binding energy per nucleon than intermediate nuclei","Heavy nuclei with A > 200 undergo spontaneous fusion rather than fission"]'::jsonb,
